[gd_scene load_steps=7 format=3]

; The compact Story HUD (2026-10-27, the user's request; first built by TG-HUDS as three glass slabs). Left: ONE glass
; slab (GlassPanelHud, 484 x ~182 at 100 %, origin (24, 20)): tier 1 the 68 px portrait frame, the 296 x 22 HP tube with
; its three 18 px block pips after it and the two 30 px status badges under it; tier 2 the 64 px Ultimate lens with the
; Defy notch on its ring, a recessed capsule holding S1 and S2 (48 px lenses) with the Momentum pips in a row under it
; (SpecialsColumn; MM-HUD), a capsule holding MOV, then a
; hairline and the time tools as a column (rewind and, in Act III, the Beacon; Time Freeze). The level title and the
; objective sit under the slab (SafeArea/TopLeft, placed in code 12 px below it, as wide as the slab less its 8 px
; indent: a long title or objective wraps instead of running into the free band). Right: the dust plate and the 64 px
; Integrity dial. BossPanel is laid out in code (640 wide at 100 %, centred in the free band). Every glyph Label keeps
; its Text and TooltipText for the tests and accessibility, its characters hidden, and the glass widget is its child.
; HeroName and FreezeSubLabel are kept hidden: their nodes and keys stay, they draw nothing
; (docs/handoffs/TG_HUDS_COMPACT.md).

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/UI/StoryHUD.cs" id="1_script"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/UI/BossPhaseNotchOverlay.cs" id="2_notches"]
